        ['q' => 'How long does an insurer have to handle my claim in Texas?', 'a' => '<p>Under the Texas Prompt Payment of Claims statute (Insurance Code Chapter 542), an insurer generally has 15 days after notice of a claim to acknowledge it, begin its investigation, and request information. It then generally has 15 business days after receiving all requested items to accept or reject the claim, with up to 45 more days if it notifies you it needs more time, and must pay within 5 business days after notifying you it accepts. These deadlines can be extended after a declared weather catastrophe. See <a href="/services/delayed-insurance-claims/">delayed insurance claims</a>.</p>'],
